IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc31-forms-periods`
IMPORT `ccc31-forms-custody`

-- ccc31-tests-custody.l4 -- tests for ccc31-forms-custody.l4 (Forms 24, 25, 26, 27, 30, 35, 39, 49 and 50).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Form (the line numbers are those of R.S.C.-1985-c.-C-46.txt),
-- before the run, and sits beside the assertion. A failing assertion is a finding, never an edit of the expected value.
-- Periods: a period begins ON the day named (ccc31-forms-periods, fork F16): 30 days from 1 January 2026 are 1 to 30 January.
-- The two seam answers are written JUST TRUE (`s 2 peace officer` and `s 2 prison` answered yes by ccc-definitions) except where a case tests them.

§ `Form 24 (Section 550) -- the peace officers (lines 18468-18471)`

-- All four recitals made out, the officer a peace officer, the place a prison: the direction stands.
#ASSERT `form 24 the peace officers are directed to arrest and convey the witness` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each recital in turn not made out ("Whereas ... This is therefore to direct you"): not covered.
#ASSERT `form 24 the peace officers are directed to arrest and convey the witness` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 24 the peace officers are directed to arrest and convey the witness` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 24 the peace officers are directed to arrest and convey the witness` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 24 the peace officers are directed to arrest and convey the witness` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The person addressed is not shown to be a peace officer (s 2 says NOTHING, or says no): not covered, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `form 24 the peace officers are directed to arrest and convey the witness` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 24 the peace officers are directed to arrest and convey the witness` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The place is not shown to be a prison.
#ASSERT `form 24 the peace officers are directed to arrest and convey the witness` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 24 the peace officers are directed to arrest and convey the witness` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Form 24 -- the keeper (line 18472): keep the witness until the trial, unless before then the witness enters into the recognizance`

-- Delivered to the keeper, the trial not yet taken place, no recognizance entered: the keeper is directed to keep the witness.
#ASSERT `form 24 the keeper is directed to keep the witness in custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The witness was never delivered to the keeper: the precept to keep has not arisen.
#ASSERT `form 24 the keeper is directed to keep the witness in custody` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "unless before that time the witness enters into the recognizance": the bar is lifted.
#ASSERT `form 24 the keeper is directed to keep the witness in custody` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "until the trial of the accused on the charge": once the trial has taken place the precept is spent.
#ASSERT `form 24 the keeper is directed to keep the witness in custody` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 24 the keeper is directed to keep the witness in custody` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Form 24 -- the duties as a regulative rule (a trace prints; it cannot be asserted on the stable binary)`

-- Expected from the text: the officer conveys and delivers, the keeper receives: the keeper is then held to SHANT release the witness (a residual obligation, no end stated).
#TRACE `form 24 the duties of the peace officers and the keeper` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `form 24 arrest if necessary, take and convey the witness to the prison and deliver them to the keeper` AT 1
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 24 receive the witness into custody in the prison` AT 2
-- Expected: the keeper releases the witness before the trial without the recognizance having been entered: BREACH BY the keeper.
#TRACE `form 24 the duties of the peace officers and the keeper` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `form 24 arrest if necessary, take and convey the witness to the prison and deliver them to the keeper` AT 1
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 24 receive the witness into custody in the prison` AT 2
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 24 release the witness` FALSE AT 5
-- Expected: the keeper releases the witness after the witness has entered into the recognizance ("unless before that time"): not a violation, the obligation stays as it was.
#TRACE `form 24 the duties of the peace officers and the keeper` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `form 24 arrest if necessary, take and convey the witness to the prison and deliver them to the keeper` AT 1
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 24 receive the witness into custody in the prison` AT 2
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 24 release the witness` TRUE AT 5

§ `Form 25 (Section 708) -- the peace officers (lines 18480-18484)`

-- All premises made out, amounts were ordered and not paid: the order stands.
#ASSERT `form 25 the peace officers are ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No amounts were ordered ("delete if not applicable"): the third recital does not stand and its absence is no bar.
#ASSERT `form 25 the peace officers are ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Amounts were ordered and the defaulter has paid them: the recital cannot be made: not covered.
#ASSERT `form 25 the peace officers are ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Each of the four other recitals in turn not made out: not covered.
#ASSERT `form 25 the peace officers are ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 25 the peace officers are ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 25 the peace officers are ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 25 the peace officers are ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The seams.
#ASSERT `form 25 the peace officers are ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 25 the peace officers are ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Form 25 -- the keeper (lines 18485-18488): the term, and "unless the sums ... are sooner paid"`

-- (a) "for the term of": 30 days from 1 January 2026 are 1 to 30 January. On 30 January the keeper is still ordered to keep; on 31 January the term has run.
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (a) for the term of` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (a) for the term of` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) has no "unless": payment does not shorten it (the text of (a) says nothing of payment).
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (a) for the term of` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE) FALSE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) same term, with "unless ... sooner paid": paid before the date asked about: the bar is lifted. Not paid: as (a), both sides of the term's end.
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (b) for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE) FALSE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (b) for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (b) for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 0, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) two terms, 30 days and 10 days, stated to run concurrently (not consecutive): custody to the end of the longer, 30 January.
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (c) for the term of and for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 10, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (c) for the term of and for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 10, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) the second term the longer (concurrent, 10 and 30 days): custody to the end of the longer, still 30 January.
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (c) for the term of and for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 10, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) "(if consecutive so state)": stated consecutive, 30 then 10 days: 1 to 30 January, then 31 January to 9 February.
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (c) for the term of and for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 10, FALSE) TRUE FALSE (Date 9 2 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (c) for the term of and for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 10, FALSE) TRUE FALSE (Date 10 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) paid while the first term is still running: the text does not say whether payment ends the first term (fork F2): not covered.
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (c) for the term of and for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 10, FALSE) TRUE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c) consecutive, paid, and the first term has run: both readings agree that nothing is left to keep the defaulter for.
#ASSERT `form 25 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` `form 25 (c) for the term of and for the term of, unless the sums and the costs and charges are sooner paid` (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 10, FALSE) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Form 25 -- "for so doing this is a sufficient warrant" (line 18485)`

#ASSERT `form 25 this is a sufficient warrant for the keeper` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 25 this is a sufficient warrant for the keeper` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Form 25 -- the duties as a regulative rule`

-- Expected: the officer conveys and delivers, the keeper receives: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `form 25 the duties of the peace officers and the keeper` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `form 25 arrest if necessary, take and convey the defaulter to the prison and deliver them to the keeper` AT 1
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 25 receive the defaulter into custody in the prison` AT 2

§ `Form 26 (Section 827) -- the peace officers (lines 18497-18500)`

#ASSERT `form 26 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the defaulter` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 26 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the defaulter` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 26 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the defaulter` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 26 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the defaulter` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 26 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the defaulter` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Form 26 -- the keeper (line 18501): the term, unless the sum AND the costs and charges are sooner paid`

-- Term 14 days from 1 January 2026: 1 to 14 January. Nothing paid: kept on 14 January, not on 15 January.
#ASSERT `form 26 the keeper is commanded to keep the defaulter in custody` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 14, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (Date 14 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 26 the keeper is commanded to keep the defaulter in custody` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 14, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The sum paid, the costs and charges not: still kept (the "unless" needs all of "the said sum and the costs and charges").
#ASSERT `form 26 the keeper is commanded to keep the defaulter in custody` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 14, FALSE) TRUE FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 26 the keeper is commanded to keep the defaulter in custody` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 14, FALSE) FALSE TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Both paid before the date asked about: "unless ... sooner paid" is met.
#ASSERT `form 26 the keeper is commanded to keep the defaulter in custody` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 14, FALSE) TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not yet delivered to the keeper.
#ASSERT `form 26 the keeper is commanded to keep the defaulter in custody` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 14, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Form 26 -- "for so doing this is a sufficient warrant", and the duties as a regulative rule`

#ASSERT `form 26 this is a sufficient warrant for the keeper` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 26 this is a sufficient warrant for the keeper` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `form 26 the duties of the peace officers and the keeper` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `form 26 take the defaulter and convey them to the prison and deliver them to the keeper` AT 1
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 26 receive the defaulter into custody in the prison` AT 2

§ `Form 27 (Section 773) -- the sheriff (lines 18509-18511) and the keeper (line 18512)`

#ASSERT `form 27 the sheriff is ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 27 the sheriff is ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 27 the sheriff is ordered to arrest and convey the defaulter` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- One month from 1 January 2026 ends at the start of 1 February: kept on 31 January, not on 1 February.
#ASSERT `form 27 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 1, 0, FALSE) FALSE (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 27 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 1, 0, FALSE) FALSE (Date 1 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "or until satisfaction is made of a judgment debt": satisfied before the date asked about (fork F3, the earlier of the two): the bar is lifted.
#ASSERT `form 27 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 1, 0, FALSE) TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not delivered, or the debt not shown to be a forfeiture debt due to Her Majesty: not covered.
#ASSERT `form 27 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 1, 0, FALSE) FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 27 the keeper is ordered to keep the defaulter in custody` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 1, 0, FALSE) FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `form 27 the duties of the sheriff and the keeper` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `form 27 arrest the defaulter and convey them to the prison and deliver them to the keeper` AT 1
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 27 receive the defaulter into custody in the prison` AT 2

§ `Form 30 (Section 537) -- the keeper is directed to have the accused before the justice (lines 18551-18552)`

#ASSERT `form 30 the keeper is directed to have the accused before the justice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 30 the keeper is directed to have the accused before the justice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 30 the keeper is directed to have the accused before the justice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The duty as a regulative rule, the hour 5 hours after the order. Expected: produced at hour 5 (the deadline is inclusive): FULFILLED.
#TRACE `form 30 the duty of the keeper` 5 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 30 have the accused before the justice at the place and hour` AT 5
-- Expected: nothing done by hour 6: BREACH BY the keeper.
#TRACE `form 30 the duty of the keeper` 5 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 6)

§ `Form 35 (Sections 570 and 806) -- the default term (lines 18758-18759)`

-- Default term 30 days from 1 January 2026 (1 to 30 January). (b), in default, nothing paid: imprisoned on 30 January, not on 31 January.
#ASSERT `form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` `form 35 (b) a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) FALSE (Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` `form 35 (b) a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) FALSE (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Paid sooner: "unless ... are sooner paid".
#ASSERT `form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` `form 35 (b) a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not in default (paid forthwith or within the time fixed): "in default of payment" is not met.
#ASSERT `form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` `form 35 (b) a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) has the same default term; (a) has none: not covered.
#ASSERT `form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` `form 35 (c) imprisonment and, in addition, a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) FALSE (Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` `form 35 (c) imprisonment and, in addition, a sum to be forfeited and paid, and costs, with imprisonment in default` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) FALSE (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 35 the imprisonment in default of payment still applies` `form 35 (a) imprisonment for the term of` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE) FALSE (Date 10 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Form 39 (Sections 519 and 550) -- the keeper is directed to release the person (lines 18795-18796)`

#ASSERT `form 39 the keeper is directed to release the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "if E.F. is detained by you for no other cause": detained for another cause, the direction does not reach.
#ASSERT `form 39 the keeper is directed to release the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not detained under the warrant or order the discharge names: not covered.
#ASSERT `form 39 the keeper is directed to release the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `form 39 the duty of the keeper` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 39 release the person` AT 1

§ `Form 49 (Section 672.57) -- Disposition of Detention (lines 18956-18965)`

-- Charged, found unfit (the first box), a hospital named, the officer a peace officer: the command stands.
#ASSERT `form 49 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the accused` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Found not criminally responsible (the second box).
#ASSERT `form 49 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the accused` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither finding made, or not charged, or the place not a prison, hospital or other appropriate place, or the officer not shown: not covered.
#ASSERT `form 49 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the accused` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 49 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the accused` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 49 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the accused` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 49 the peace officers are commanded to take and convey the accused` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- The keeper's precept: "until the accused is delivered by due course of law".
#ASSERT `form 49 the keeper is directed to keep the accused in custody` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 49 the keeper is directed to keep the accused in custody` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 49 the keeper is directed to keep the accused in custody` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The conditions: "while in your (prison, hospital or other appropriate place)".
#ASSERT `form 49 the accused is subject to the condition` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 49 the accused is subject to the condition` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 49 the accused is subject to the condition` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The delegated powers.
#ASSERT `form 49 the keeper holds the delegated power` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 49 the keeper holds the delegated power` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `form 49 the duties of the peace officers and the keeper` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `form 49 take the accused in custody and convey them to the place and deliver them to the keeper` AT 1
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 49 receive the accused into custody in the place` AT 2

§ `Form 50 (Subsection 672.7(2)) -- Placement Decision (lines 18975-18985)`

-- All four recitals made out; the box ticked is the court's warrant: the command to execute the court's warrant stands.
#ASSERT `form 50 the keeper is commanded to execute the warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The box ticked is the court's; asked about the Review Board's warrant: not commanded by this Form (the other alternative), not covered.
#ASSERT `form 50 the keeper is commanded to execute the warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` `form 50 the warrant of committal issued herewith by the Review Board` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 50 the keeper is commanded to execute the warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `form 50 the warrant of committal issued herewith by the Review Board` `form 50 the warrant of committal issued herewith by the Review Board` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each recital in turn not made out.
#ASSERT `form 50 the keeper is commanded to execute the warrant` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 50 the keeper is commanded to execute the warrant` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 50 the keeper is commanded to execute the warrant` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 50 the keeper is commanded to execute the warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` `form 50 the warrant of committal issued by the court, according to its terms` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `form 50 the duty of the keeper` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 50 execute the warrant` AT 1
